# Files a Linux shell or a Linux container reads keep LF endings on every
# checkout, a Windows one with core.autocrlf=true included. A run-*.sh with CRLF
# endings fails on its first line ("bad interpreter") and the indexer it starts
# crash-loops. The rest here are built or parsed on Linux and stay LF to match.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.githooks/*     text eol=lf
